      "source": [
        "## Network"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "21Ap___kCDun"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0ch67jsSru0O"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "class VelocityNet(nn.Module):\n",
        "  def __init__(self, hidden_dim=128):\n",
        "    super().__init__()\n",
        "    # Input is x (2 dims) + t (1 dim), so 3 dims\n",
        "    self.net = nn.Sequential(\n",
        "        nn.Linear(3, hidden_dim),\n",
        "        nn.SiLU(),\n",
        "        nn.Linear(hidden_dim, hidden_dim),\n",
        "        nn.SiLU(),\n",
        "        nn.Linear(hidden_dim, hidden_dim),\n",
        "        nn.SiLU(),\n",
        "        nn.Linear(hidden_dim, hidden_dim),\n",
        "        nn.SiLU(),\n",
        "        nn.Linear(hidden_dim, hidden_dim),\n",
        "        nn.SiLU(),\n",
        "        nn.Linear(hidden_dim, 2), # Output is a 2D velocity vector\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "  def forward(self, x, t):\n",
        "    # x: [B, 2], t[B, 1]\n",
        "    inputs = torch.cat([x, t], dim=-1) # this is not what we do for images or video, but for this simple case, it's enough\n",
        "    return self.net(inputs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "1xfFLjtCs0r_"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Flow Matching Objective\n",
        "\n",
        "First, we sample points $X_1 ∈ \\mathbb{R}^2$ and labels $Y \\in \\{0, 1\\}$ from our Two Moons target data distribution $q$:\n",
        "\n",
        "$(X_1, Y) ∼ q_{data}$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "Then we take a sample with the same dimensions from a known simple distribution $p$, in our case a Gaussian:\n",
        "\n",
        "$X_0 \\sim p_0 = \\mathcal{N}(0, I)$\n",
        "  \n",
        "We sample a random timestep $t$ from the uniform distribution $\\mathcal{U}$:  \n",
        "\n",
        "$t \\sim \\mathcal{U}[0, 1]$\n",
        "\n",
        "For Optimal Transport Conditional Flow Matching (OT-CFM), the interpolated path at time t between Gaussian noise $X_0$ and target data $X_1$ is a simple linear blend:\n",
        "\n",
        "$X_t = (1 - t)X_0 + tX_1 = X_0 + t(X_1 - X_0)$\n",
        "\n",
        "The exact target velocity (the direction and the magnitude pointing directly from $x_0$ to $x_1$) is:\n",
        "\n",
        "$U_t = \\frac{dX_t}{dt} = X_1 - X_0$\n",
        "\n",
        "We take the loss between the predicted and target velocities:\n",
        "\n",
        "$\\mathcal{L}(θ) = \\mathbb{E}[\\|v_θ(X_t, t) - U_t\\|^2]$\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Code"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "VnAWdgIECKLu"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "A5UhNOmKtqG1"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def compute_loss(network, x1):\n",
        "  batch_size: int = x1.shape[0] # B: 512\n",
        "\n",
        "  # 1. Sample standard Gaussian noise (x0)\n",
        "  x0 = torch.randn_like(x1)\n",
        "\n",
        "  # 2. Sample random times uniformly between 0 and 1\n",
        "  t = torch.rand((batch_size, 1))\n",
        "\n",
        "  # 3. Compute the conditional flow path (linear interpolation)\n",
        "  xt = (1.0 - t) * x0 + t * x1\n",
        "\n",
        "  # 4. Target velocity is simply the straight line path\n",
        "  ut = x1 - x0\n",
        "\n",
        "  # 5. Predict velocity with the neural network\n",
        "  vt = network(xt, t)\n",
        "\n",
        "  # 6. Mean Squared Error loss matches the predicted flow to target flow\n",
        "  loss = torch.mean((vt - ut) ** 2)\n",
        "  return loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "a-CoSXbg-aPI"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Training Loop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "jxfcYXpzugbx"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "network = VelocityNet(hidden_dim=128)\n",
        "optimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(network.parameters(), lr=1e-3)\n",
        "\n",
        "steps = 5000\n",
        "batch_size = 512\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "h7mvOMlqw335",
        "outputId": "225c6d16-8d52-48a3-ee0b-89b5e2a2ead4"
